      "output": "```js\nconst TUNING = {\n  car: {\n    maxSpeed: 62,        // m/s top speed without boost\n    accel: 16,           // m/s² at full throttle\n    brake: 32,           // m/s² braking\n    drag: 0.0024,        // per m: a -= drag*v*|v|\n    rolling: 1.2,        // m/s² constant coast loss\n    steerRate: 2.4,      // rad/s yaw at low speed\n    steerAtSpeed: 0.42,  // steer multiplier at maxSpeed, lerped linearly from 1 at 0 m/s\n    grip: 9,             // 1/s lateral-velocity decay\n    driftGrip: 2.4,      // 1/s lateral decay while drifting\n    driftSteer: 1.45,    // steer multiplier while drifting\n    boostFill: 0.34,     // meter (0–1) per s of drift\n    boostSpeed: 1.24,    // boost top speed = maxSpeed*1.24 (76.9 m/s)\n    boostSeconds: 2.6,   // s of boost from a full meter\n    wallSlow: 0.6,       // speed multiplier on wall hit\n    bump: 5              // m/s impulse split on car contact\n  },\n  ai: [\n    { name: \"VOLT\",  color: \"#ff2fd6\", skill: 1.02, aggression: 0.75 },\n    { name: \"NOVA\",  color: \"#00f0ff\", skill: 1.01, aggression: 0.55 },\n    { name: \"RAZOR\", color: \"#ffe600\", skill: 1.00, aggression: 0.85 },\n    { name: \"HALO\",  color: \"#39ff14\", skill: 0.99, aggression: 0.35 },\n    { name: \"ECHO\",  color: \"#ff6a00\", skill: 0.97, aggression: 0.5 }\n  ],\n  race: { laps: 3, countdown: 3, rubberBand: { range: 80, behind: 0.08, ahead: 0.04 } },\n  camera: {\n    distance: 7.5,       // m behind car\n    height: 2.6,         // m above car\n    lag: 0.12,           // s follow smoothing\n    fovBoost: 12         // degrees added at full boost\n  }\n};\n```\n\n1. **Race flow.** The title screen leads to a 3‑2‑1‑GO countdown with controls locked. The race runs 3 laps. Results show a podium as soon as the player finishes; unfinished rivals are ranked by progress. Race again resets to the countdown.\n2. **Drift.**\n   - **Start:** Space is held with steer input above 0.3 at more than 18 m/s. Grip switches to driftGrip and steering is multiplied by driftSteer.\n   - **Filling the meter:** the meter gains boostFill·dt while slip angle exceeds 0.15 rad.\n   - **End:** the drift ends when Space is released, speed falls below 12 m/s or the car hits a wall. The meter is kept.\n   - **Boost:** Shift with a meter above 0 raises top speed to maxSpeed·boostSpeed for boostSeconds·meter.\n3. **Laps and positions.**\n   - About 30 ordered checkpoint gates, roughly 60 m apart, cover the 1.8 km loop. Only the next expected gate counts, so skipped gates count for nothing.\n   - Crossing gate 0 after the last gate counts a lap.\n   - Position is sorted by laps·30 + gate + fraction to the next gate.\n4. **Wrong way.** \"WRONG WAY\" shows after 1.5 s with heading·track tangent below −0.3 at more than 5 m/s. It clears after 1 s facing forward.\n5. **Rubber band.** Beyond 80 m behind the player, a rival's speed bonus ramps linearly to +8% at 240 m. Beyond 80 m ahead, its penalty ramps to −4% at 240 m.\n6. **Pacing targets.**\n   - A good drifting lap takes about 52.5 s.\n   - VOLT laps in about 53.8 s and finishes roughly 4 s behind a good player.\n   - A player who never drifts laps in about 55 s and finishes behind VOLT and NOVA.\n7. **Not verified.** No race simulation or playtest was run, so the lap times, gaps and the non-drifter outcome above are calculated estimates. Confirm them on the real track and adjust ai skill first."
