      "output": "# Neon Circuit — Track layout\n\n**Status: not executed.** I wrote this code but did not run it, so the \"Not verified\" list at the end still needs confirming in the browser.\n\n## How the loop runs\n\n- **Long straight (pts 0–4):** about 380 m along z ≈ −205, heading +x. The grid and start line are at point 1.\n- **Fast banked sweeper (pts 5–10):** a long right-hander round the east end, banked up to 0.16 rad.\n- **S-section (pts 12–16):** a right–left wiggle along the north side.\n- **Tunnel (pts 16–19):** across the north-west corner.\n- **Hairpin (pts 21–24):** at the west end, radius about 31 m, then a right–left kink (pts 25–27) back onto the straight.\n\n## Conventions\n\n- **Direction:** the loop runs clockwise seen from above, so the corners are right-handers.\n- **Left normal:** `(nx, nz) = (tz, −tx)`.\n- **Bank:** positive bank raises the left edge. The left edge sits at `y + w·sin(bank)` and the right edge at `y − w·sin(bank)`.\n- **Sign side:** `1` is on the left (+n) side, which is the outside of these corners. `−1` is on the right.\n- **Extra data on the samples array:** `samples.total` is the loop length, `samples.step` is the sample spacing (about 2 m), and `samples.pointS[i]` is the `s` of control point `i`. Use `pointS` to turn `checkpoints`, `tunnel` and `signs` into sample positions.\n- **Gates for the ~30 race-rule checkpoints:** take every 30th sample (about 60 m apart).\n- **Towers:**\n  - There are two rings of 24 outside the loop.\n  - The inner ring is 45–68 m tall and the outer ring, towards the horizon, is 105–150 m.\n  - By hand calculation, each tower is at least about 70 m from the centreline.\n\n```js\nconst TRACK={points:[[-190,-200,9,0],[-95,-205,10,0],[0,-205,10,0],[95,-205,10,0],[190,-200,9,.02],[265,-175,9,.08],[310,-120,9,.14],[330,-50,9.5,.16],[325,25,9.5,.16],[300,95,9,.14],[250,150,9,.08],[185,180,8.5,.02],[115,190,8,0],[55,165,8,-.04],[0,140,8,-.06],[-55,160,8,.04],[-105,200,8,.06],[-165,212,7.5,0],[-225,200,7.5,0],[-265,170,8,.02],[-300,125,8,.03],[-325,75,8,.05],[-345,40,7,.08],[-350,5,7,.08],[-325,-15,7,.06],[-285,-30,8,-.03],[-275,-95,8.5,.02],[-245,-165,9,.04]],\nstart:1,checkpoints:[1,5,8,11,14,18,22,26],tunnel:[16,19],\ntowers:[[440,0,22,20,55,.83],[425,83,18,22,48,.52],[381,160,24,18,62,.9],[311,226,20,20,45,.58],[220,277,22,24,58,.78],[114,309,18,18,66,.5],[0,320,26,20,52,.86],[-114,309,20,22,60,.55],[-220,277,18,18,47,.92],[-311,226,24,20,64,.6],[-381,160,20,24,50,.8],[-425,83,22,18,57,.53],[-440,0,18,20,68,.88],[-425,-83,24,22,49,.56],[-381,-160,20,18,61,.82],[-311,-226,22,20,54,.5],[-220,-277,18,24,46,.9],[-114,-309,26,20,63,.58],[0,-320,20,18,51,.85],[114,-309,22,22,59,.52],[220,-277,18,20,48,.79],[311,-226,24,18,65,.55],[381,-160,20,22,53,.91],[425,-83,22,20,60,.6],\n[575,56,30,28,120,.55],[536,165,26,30,135,.85],[460,262,32,26,105,.5],[353,341,28,32,145,.8],[222,397,30,28,115,.58],[76,426,34,30,150,.9],[-76,426,28,26,125,.53],[-222,397,32,30,140,.83],[-353,341,26,28,110,.6],[-460,262,30,32,148,.88],[-536,165,28,26,118,.5],[-575,56,32,30,132,.8],[-575,-56,26,28,108,.56],[-536,-165,30,26,142,.86],[-460,-262,28,32,116,.52],[-353,-341,34,28,138,.9],[-222,-397,26,30,112,.58],[-76,-426,30,26,146,.82],[76,-426,28,32,122,.55],[222,-397,32,28,136,.87],[353,-341,26,26,109,.5],[460,-262,30,30,144,.8],[536,-165,28,28,119,.6],[575,-56,32,26,130,.85]],\nsigns:[[5,1],[7,1],[9,1],[14,-1],[16,1],[21,1],[22,1],[23,1],[25,-1],[27,1]]};\n\nfunction sampleTrack(T){const P=T.points,n=P.length,st=T.start|0,m=Math,G=i=>P[(i+st)%n],d=[],ps=[],H=(a,b)=>m.max(m.sqrt(m.hypot(b[0]-a[0],b[1]-a[1])),1e-3);\nfor(let i=0;i<n;i++){const a=G(i+n-1),b=G(i),c=G(i+1),e=G(i+2),t1=H(a,b),t2=t1+H(b,c),t3=t2+H(c,e);\nfor(let j=0;j<40;j++){const u=j/40,t=t1+(t2-t1)*u,h=u*u*(3-2*u),f=k=>{const A1=((t1-t)*a[k]+t*b[k])/t1,A2=((t2-t)*b[k]+(t-t1)*c[k])/(t2-t1),A3=((t3-t)*c[k]+(t-t2)*e[k])/(t3-t2),B1=((t2-t)*A1+t*A2)/t2,B2=((t3-t)*A2+(t-t1)*A3)/(t3-t1);return((t2-t)*B1+(t-t1)*B2)/(t2-t1)};\nd.push([f(0),f(1),b[2]+(c[2]-b[2])*h,b[3]+(c[3]-b[3])*h,j?-1:(i+st)%n])}}\nd.push(d[0]);const L=[0];for(let i=1;i<d.length;i++){L[i]=L[i-1]+m.hypot(d[i][0]-d[i-1][0],d[i][1]-d[i-1][1]);if(d[i-1][4]>=0)ps[d[i-1][4]]=L[i-1]}\nconst len=L[L.length-1],N=m.round(len/2),ds=len/N,S=[];let k=0;\nfor(let i=0;i<N;i++){const s=i*ds;while(L[k+1]<s)k++;const p=d[k],q=d[k+1],r=(s-L[k])/(L[k+1]-L[k]||1),g=v=>p[v]+(q[v]-p[v])*r,u=s/len*2*m.PI;\nS.push({x:g(0),z:g(1),y:2.5*m.sin(u)+1.5*m.sin(3*u+1),tx:0,tz:0,nx:0,nz:0,w:g(2),bank:g(3),s})}\nS.forEach((o,i)=>{const A=S[(i+N-1)%N],B=S[(i+1)%N],x=B.x-A.x,z=B.z-A.z,l=m.hypot(x,z)||1;o.tx=x/l;o.tz=z/l;o.nx=o.tz;o.nz=-o.tx});\nS.total=len;S.step=ds;S.pointS=ps;return S}\n```\n\n**Size:** the code is about 3.9 k characters, under the 4,500 limit.\n\n**Calling it:** `const samples = sampleTrack(TRACK);`. Nothing runs at the top level.\n\n## Not verified\n\n- **Lap length:** worked out by hand from the control polygon (about 1,853 m). The spline should come out at roughly 1.86 km, but nobody has read `samples.total` yet.\n- **No self-crossing:** checked only by eye. Plot the samples, especially the hairpin and the kink at pts 21–27, and the S-section.\n- **Tower clearance:** the ≥25 m gap from the road edge comes from hand calculation. To confirm it, check every tower footprint against every sample, using distance minus `w`.\n- **Closure:** smooth closure at s = 0 comes from the method (a periodic spline, periodic height and a centripetal C¹ fit). It has not been checked visually.\n- **Pacing:** fit with the TUNING lap times (about 52.5 s at about 1.86 km) has not been playtested."
